</respprops>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>197</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>598</cx>
<cy>265</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1768211Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1768211Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;span.text1768211Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#0000ff; font-weight:bold; text-decoration:underline;}&#x0A;span.text1768211Font4 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#000000; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:11px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1768211Font1&quot;  &gt;Dupuytren&apos;s contracture involves overexpression of types I and III collagen, associated with a complex string of events including myofibroblast proliferation (resulting in nodule formation), extracellular matrix remodeling combined with immune mediated and mechanically-triggered actin microfilament contraction (resulting in shortening fascial bands) and nodule regression (resulting in the formation of inelastic, tendon-like cords or digital flexion contractures). Individuals at increased risk for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture include older male Caucasians of Northern European descent, and it typically presents during the 50s age range and onward. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1768211Font2&quot;  &gt;Please view the video on the pathophysiology of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture &lt;/span &gt;&lt;a href=&quot;##Action 1836828&quot;  &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1768211Font3&quot;  &gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1768211Font4&quot;  &gt;.&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1768211Font1&quot;  &gt; &lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf3\cb1\ulc3 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf3\cb1\ulc3\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f2\cf3\cb1\ulc3 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\sa160\ql Dupuytren&apos;s contracture involves overexpression of types I and III collagen, associated with a complex string of events including myofibroblast proliferation (resulting in nodule formation), extracellular matrix remodeling &#x0A;combined with immune mediated and mechanically-triggered actin microfilament contraction (resulting in shortening fascial bands) and nodule regression (resulting in the formation of inelastic, tendon-like cords or digital flexion contractures). Individuals &#x0A;at increased risk for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture include older male Caucasians of Northern\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1  European descent, and it typically presents during the 50s age range and onward.  \plain\f1\fs24\par\sa120\b Please view the video on the &#x0A;pathophysiology of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture \cf2\sshlink\ul{\field{\fldinst HYPERLINK &quot;##Action 1836828&quot;}{\fldrslt here}}\cf3\sshlink0\ul0 .\plain\f1\fs24  \line\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Dupuytren&apos;s contracture involves overexpression of types I and III collagen, associated with a complex string of events including myofibroblast proliferation (resulting in nodule formation), extracellular matrix remodeling combined with immune mediated and mechanically-triggered actin microfilament contraction (resulting in shortening fascial bands) and nodule regression (resulting in the formation of inelastic, tendon-like cords or digital flexion contractures). Individuals at increased risk for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture include older male Caucasians of Northern European descent, and it typically presents during the 50s age range and onward.  &#x0A;Please view the video on the pathophysiology of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture here. &#x0F;</raw>
<numoflines>11</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
