<cx>621</cx>
<cy>127</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1857395Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1857395Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#0000ff; text-decoration:underline;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1857395Font1&quot;  &gt;XIAFLEX should only be administered by a healthcare provider (HCP) experienced in injection procedures of the hand and in the treatment of patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture who have been trained on the administration of XIAFLEX for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. Remind HCPs that their expertise helps define the patient&apos;s experience. HCPs can go to&lt;/span &gt;&lt;a href=&quot;##Action 1887407&quot;  &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1857395Font2&quot;  &gt; www.xiaflex.com/XTRA&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1857395Font1&quot;  &gt; for resources to help refine their XIAFLEX injection technique. The website also provides materials needed to integrate XIAFLEX into their practice. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf3\cb1\ulc3 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 XIAFLEX should only be administered by a healthcare provider (HCP) experienced in injection procedures of the hand and in the treatment of patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture who have been trained on &#x0A;the administration of XIAFLEX for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. Remind HCPs that their expertise helps define the patient&apos;s experience. HCPs can go to{\field\fldlock{\*\fldinst MERGEFIELD \cf2\sshlink\ul  HYPERLINK &quot;##Action 1887407&quot; }{\fldrslt\cf2\sshlink\ul &#x0A; www.xiaflex.com/XTRA}} for resources to help refine their XIAFLEX injection technique. The website also provides materials needed to integrate XIAFLEX into their practice. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿XIAFLEX should only be administered by a healthcare provider (HCP) experienced in injection procedures of the hand and in the treatment of patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture who have been trained on the administration of XIAFLEX for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. Remind HCPs that their expertise helps define the patient&apos;s experience. HCPs can go to www.xiaflex.com/XTRA for resources to help refine their XIAFLEX injection technique. The website also provides materials needed to integrate XIAFLEX into their practice. </raw>
<numoflines>7</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
