<cssclasses>hideMe a_title</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1864030Font1 { font-size:21px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#000000; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864030Font1&quot;  &gt;Dosing Note&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\cf2\fs32\b Dosing Note\line\plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Dosing Note&#x0F;</raw>
<numoflines>2</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
<text id="1864031" parent="1864025" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" defaulttext="none">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769445192</lastupdated>
<respprops>
<tabletportrait>
<text>
<possize>
<size>
<cx>466</cx>
<cy>152</cy>
</size>
</possize>
</text>
</tabletportrait>
</respprops>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>218</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>611</cx>
<cy>208</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1864031Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864031Font1&quot;  &gt;This section summarizes the injection procedure for XIAFLEX. HCPs can administer XIAFLEX in their office, and they must have completed training before injecting XIAFLEX. Local anesthesia may be used only during the finger extension procedure. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864031Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864031Font1&quot;  &gt;On Day 1, HCPs inject XIAFLEX. The full clinical dose of XIAFLEX is 0.58 mg per injection into a palpable cord with a contracture of MP or PIP joints. Each vial of XIAFLEX and sterile diluent should only be used for a single injection. Up to 2 joints on the same hand may be treated during a single treatment visit. Each joint requires a separate vial of XIAFLEX and sterile diluent. If a patient has other palpable cords with contractures of MP or PIP joints, inject those cords at another treatment visit approximately 4 weeks apart. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil \fcharset2 Wingdings;}{\f3 \froman \fcharset2 Symbol;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 This section summarizes the injection procedure for XIAFLEX. HCPs can administer XIAFLEX in their office, and they must have completed training before injecting XIAFLEX. Local anesthesia may be used only &#x0A;during the finger extension procedure.  \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 On Day 1, HCPs inject XIAFLEX. The full clinical dose of XIAFLEX is 0.58 mg per injection into a palpable cord with a contracture of MP or PIP joints. Each vial of &#x0A;XIAFLEX and sterile diluent should only be used for a single injection. Up to 2 joints on the same hand may be treated during a single treatment visit. Each joint requires a separate vial of XIAFLEX and sterile diluent. If a patient has other palpable &#x0A;cords with contractures of MP or PIP joints, inject those cords at another treatment visit approximately 4 weeks apart.  \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿This section summarizes the injection procedure for XIAFLEX. HCPs can administer XIAFLEX in their office, and they must have completed training before injecting XIAFLEX. Local anesthesia may be used only during the finger extension procedure.  &#x0A;On Day 1, HCPs inject XIAFLEX. The full clinical dose of XIAFLEX is 0.58 mg per injection into a palpable cord with a contracture of MP or PIP joints. Each vial of XIAFLEX and sterile diluent should only be used for a single injection. Up to 2 joints on the same hand may be treated during a single treatment visit. Each joint requires a separate vial of XIAFLEX and sterile diluent. If a patient has other palpable cords with contractures of MP or PIP joints, inject those cords at another treatment visit approximately 4 weeks apart.  </raw>
<numoflines>11</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
