<html>span.text1864171Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:normal;}&#x0A;li.text1864171Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:normal; font-style:normal; text-decoration:normal;}&#x0A;span.text1864171Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; text-decoration:normal;}&#x0A;li.text1864171Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; text-decoration:normal;}&#x0A;span.text1864171Font4 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#0000ff; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; text-decoration:underline;}&#x0A;li.text1864171Font4 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#0000ff; font-weight:bold; font-style:normal; text-decoration:underline;}&#x0A;&lt;ol  start=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;list-style-position:outside;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;Load 0.25 mL of reconstituted XIAFLEX 0.58 mg solution into a new, 1-mL hubless syringe with 0.01-mL graduations with a permanently fixed, 27-gauge Â½-inch needle. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;To perform the injection, the patient&apos;s hand is secured in the injector&apos;s nondominant hand while tension is simultaneously applied to the cord. The dominant hand is used to carefully place the needle into the cord, taking care the needle does not exit the cord; a small amount of passive motion may be applied to the distal interphalangeal joint to confirm the needle has avoided the flexor tendon (if tendon insertion is suspected or paresthesia is noted by the patient, the needle should be withdrawn and repositioned into the cord). &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;After needle placement has been confirmed, approximately one-third of the dose is injected; some resistance will be noted if the needle has been properly located. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;Next, the needle is repositioned approximately 2 to 3 mm distal to the initial injection site, and the second one-third of the dose is administered. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;For the final dose, the needle is repositioned approximately 2 to 3 mm proximal to the initial injection site, and the last one-third of the dose is delivered. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;If a second dose is to be administered in the same hand during a single visit, a new syringe and vial of reconstituted solution is used for each set of injections. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;If 2 doses are to be administered in the same hand during a single visit, the affected finger in the most medial aspect should be injected first, with the injections continuing toward the lateral aspect; if both doses are to be administered to 2 joints in the same finger, the affected joint in the most proximal aspect of the finger should be injected first and continue toward the distal aspect. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;After the last injection, the patient&apos;s hand should be dressed in a soft, bulky gauze. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;The patient should be instructed to limit motion of the treated finger(s) and to keep the hand elevated until bedtime. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;The patient should be instructed not to manipulate the injected cord(s) and to return to their HCP one day following the injection for follow-up and finger extension procedure(s) as indicated. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;li  class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;line-height:1.127;position:relative;padding-left:10px;list-style-type:lower-alpha;margin-left:21px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot;  &gt;Discard any unused reconstituted solution and/or diluent. Do not store, pool, or use any vials containing unused reconstituted solution or diluent. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/li &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/ol &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font3&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:8px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font3&quot;  &gt;Please view the video clip on the injection procedure &lt;/span &gt;&lt;a href=&quot;##Action 1888887&quot;  &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font4&quot;  &gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font3&quot;  &gt;. &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1864171Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \froman \fcharset2 Symbol;}{\f3 \fnil \fcharset2 Wingdings;}{\f4 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf3\cb1\ulc3 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf3\cb1\ulc3\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f4\cf3\cb1\ulc3 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;{\*\listtable&#x0A;{\list\listtemplateid1&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc4\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;00.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;01.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc1\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;02.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc2\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;03.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc3\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;04.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc4\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;05.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;06.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc1\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;07.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc2\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;08.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listname DefaultList;}\listid1768492093&#x0A;}&#x0A;{\list\listtemplateid2&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc4\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;00.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;01.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc1\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;02.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc2\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;03.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc3\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;04.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc4\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;05.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;06.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc1\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;07.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listlevel\levelnfc2\levelfollow0\levelstartat1{\leveltext \&apos;02\&apos;08.}{\levelnumbers \&apos;01}}&#x0A;{\listname DefaultList;}\listid1769445298&#x0A;}&#x0A;}&#x0A;{\*\listoverridetable&#x0A;{\listoverride\listid1769445298\listoverridecount0\ls1}&#x0A;}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\pard\s0{\pntext\pard\plain\f1\fs24 a.\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlbody\pnstart1\ls1\ilvl0\pnhang{\pntxta \&apos;2e}}\ls1\ilvl0\fi-450\li450\sa120\ql Load 0.25 mL of reconstituted XIAFLEX 0.58 mg solution into a new, 1-mL hubless syringe with 0.01-mL &#x0A;graduations with a permanently fixed, 27-gauge \plain\f1\fs24\u189 \&apos;bd\plain\f1\fs24 -inch needle.  \par To perform the injection, the patient&apos;s hand is secured in the injector&apos;s nondominant hand while tension is simultaneously applied to the cord. The &#x0A;dominant hand is used to carefully place the needle into the cord, taking care the needle does not exit the cord; a small amount of passive motion may be applied to the distal interphalangeal joint to confirm the needle has avoided the flexor tendon (if &#x0A;tendon insertion is suspected or paresthesia is noted by the patient, the needle should be withdrawn and repositioned into the cord). \par After needle placement has been confirmed, approximately one-third of the dose is injected; some resistance will &#x0A;be noted if the needle has been properly located. \par Next, the needle is repositioned approximately 2 to 3 mm distal to the initial injection site, and the second one-third of the dose is administered. \par For the final dose, the needle is repositioned &#x0A;approximately 2 to 3 mm proximal to the initial injection site, and the last one-third of the dose is delivered. \par If a second dose is to be administered in the same hand during a single visit, a new syringe and vial of reconstituted solution is used &#x0A;for each set of injections. \par If 2 doses are to be administered in the same hand during a single visit, the affected finger in the most medial aspect should be injected first, with the injections continuing toward the lateral aspect; if both doses &#x0A;are to be administered to 2 joints in the same finger, the affected joint in the most proximal aspect of the finger should be injected first and continue toward the distal aspect. \par After the last injection, the patient&apos;s hand should be dressed in &#x0A;a soft, bulky gauze. \par The patient should be instructed to limit motion of the treated finger(s) and to keep the hand elevated until bedtime. \par The patient should be instructed not to manipulate the injected cord(s) and to return to their HCP one &#x0A;day following the injection for follow-up and finger extension procedure(s) as indicated. \par Discard any unused reconstituted solution and/or diluent. Do not store, pool, or use any vials containing unused reconstituted solution or diluent. \par\pard\s0\ql\b\par\sa120\plain\f1\fs24\b &#x0A;Please view the video clip on the injection procedure {\field\fldlock{\*\fldinst MERGEFIELD \lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\sshlink\ul  HYPERLINK &quot;##Action 1888887&quot; }{\fldrslt\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\sshlink\ul here}}. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Load 0.25 mL of reconstituted XIAFLEX 0.58 mg solution into a new, 1-mL hubless syringe with 0.01-mL graduations with a permanently fixed, 27-gauge ½-inch needle.  &#x0A;To perform the injection, the patient&apos;s hand is secured in the injector&apos;s nondominant hand while tension is simultaneously applied to the cord. The dominant hand is used to carefully place the needle into the cord, taking care the needle does not exit the cord; a small amount of passive motion may be applied to the distal interphalangeal joint to confirm the needle has avoided the flexor tendon (if tendon insertion is suspected or paresthesia is noted by the patient, the needle should be withdrawn and repositioned into the cord). &#x0A;After needle placement has been confirmed, approximately one-third of the dose is injected; some resistance will be noted if the needle has been properly located. &#x0A;Next, the needle is repositioned approximately 2 to 3 mm distal to the initial injection site, and the second one-third of the dose is administered. &#x0A;For the final dose, the needle is repositioned approximately 2 to 3 mm proximal to the initial injection site, and the last one-third of the dose is delivered. &#x0A;If a second dose is to be administered in the same hand during a single visit, a new syringe and vial of reconstituted solution is used for each set of injections. &#x0A;If 2 doses are to be administered in the same hand during a single visit, the affected finger in the most medial aspect should be injected first, with the injections continuing toward the lateral aspect; if both doses are to be administered to 2 joints in the same finger, the affected joint in the most proximal aspect of the finger should be injected first and continue toward the distal aspect. &#x0A;After the last injection, the patient&apos;s hand should be dressed in a soft, bulky gauze. &#x0A;The patient should be instructed to limit motion of the treated finger(s) and to keep the hand elevated until bedtime. &#x0A;The patient should be instructed not to manipulate the injected cord(s) and to return to their HCP one day following the injection for follow-up and finger extension procedure(s) as indicated. &#x0A;Discard any unused reconstituted solution and/or diluent. Do not store, pool, or use any vials containing unused reconstituted solution or diluent. &#x0A;Please view the video clip on the injection procedure here. </raw>
