<text id="1806680" parent="1806674" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" publishasimage="true" defaulttext="none">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769448922</lastupdated>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>213</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>605</cx>
<cy>217</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1806680Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1806680Font1&quot;  &gt;In the Dupuytren&apos;s contracture trials (Studies 1 and 2), 15% of XIAFLEX-treated patients compared to 1% of placebo-treated patients had mild allergic reactions (pruritus) after up to 3 injections during the controlled portions of the trials. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1806680Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1806680Font1&quot;  &gt;Because XIAFLEX contains foreign proteins, severe allergic reactions to XIAFLEX can occur. Anaphylaxis was reported in a postmarketing trial (Study 3) in 1 patient treated for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture who had prior exposure to XIAFLEX. Some patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture developed IgE-anti-drug antibodies in greater proportions and higher titers with successive injections. HCPs should be prepared to address severe allergic reactions following XIAFLEX injections. These include anaphylaxis, which is a sudden, severe allergic reaction that occurs within minutes and may recur hours later. Anaphylaxis can be local or systemic and may be life-threatening. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf3\cb1\ulc3 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 In the Dupuytren&apos;s contracture trials (Studies 1 and 2), 15% of XIAFLEX-treated patients compared to 1% of placebo-treated patients had mild allergic reactions (pruritus) after up to 3 injections during &#x0A;the controlled portions of the trials. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 Because XIAFLEX contains foreign proteins, severe allergic reactions to XIAFLEX can occur. Anaphylaxis was reported in a postmarketing trial (Study 3) in 1 patient &#x0A;treated for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture who had prior exposure to XIAFLEX. Some patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture developed IgE-anti-drug antibodies in greater proportions and higher titers with successive injections. HCPs should be prepared to address &#x0A;severe allergic reactions following XIAFLEX injections. These include anaphylaxis, which is a sudden, severe allergic reaction that occurs within minutes and may recur hours later. Anaphylaxis can be local or systemic and may be life-threatening.  \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿In the Dupuytren&apos;s contracture trials (Studies 1 and 2), 15% of XIAFLEX-treated patients compared to 1% of placebo-treated patients had mild allergic reactions (pruritus) after up to 3 injections during the controlled portions of the trials. &#x0A;Because XIAFLEX contains foreign proteins, severe allergic reactions to XIAFLEX can occur. Anaphylaxis was reported in a postmarketing trial (Study 3) in 1 patient treated for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture who had prior exposure to XIAFLEX. Some patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture developed IgE-anti-drug antibodies in greater proportions and higher titers with successive injections. HCPs should be prepared to address severe allergic reactions following XIAFLEX injections. These include anaphylaxis, which is a sudden, severe allergic reaction that occurs within minutes and may recur hours later. Anaphylaxis can be local or systemic and may be life-threatening.  </raw>
<numoflines>12</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
