<html>span.text1871073Font1 { font-size:21px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#000000; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;span.text1871073Font2 { font-size:13px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#000000; font-style:italic;}&#x0A;span.text1871073Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.192&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.192;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871073Font1&quot;  &gt;Safety Note&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871073Font2&quot;  &gt;Scroll for more information.&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871073Font3&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\cf2\fs32\b Safety Note\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\line\fs20\b0\i Scroll for more information.\plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Safety Note&#x0F;Scroll for more information.</raw>
<numoflines>2</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
<text id="1871074" parent="1871068" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" defaulttext="none" verticalscroll="true">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769449076</lastupdated>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>213</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>622</cx>
<cy>192</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1871074Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871074Font1&quot;  &gt;Because clinical studies are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical studies of a drug cannot be directly compared to the rates in the clinical studies of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871074Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871074Font1&quot;  &gt;In the controlled and uncontrolled portion of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture XIAFLEX clinical studies, of the 1082 patients who received 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX (2630 XIAFLEX injections), there were 3 patients (0.3%) who experienced a flexor tendon rupture of the treated finger within 7 days of the injection. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871074Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1871074Font1&quot;  &gt;This section of the XIAFLEX PI describes reactions that occurred during the clinical trials program for XIAFLEX in Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. Studies 1 and 2 (CORD I and CORD II) were the clinical trials that supported the approval of XIAFLEX for the treatment of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. In Study 1 and Study 2, patients were treated with up to 3 injections of 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX or placebo with approximately 4-week intervals between injections. Patients had finger extension procedures the day after injection, if needed, to facilitate disruption of the cord. The 2 studies were composed of 374 patients; 249 received 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX and 125 received placebo. Participants had a mean age of 63 years; 100% of participants were white, ~80% were male, and ~20% were female. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil \fcharset2 Wingdings;}{\f3 \froman \fcharset2 Symbol;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 Because clinical studies are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical studies of a drug cannot be directly compared to the rates in the clinical studies &#x0A;of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 In the controlled and uncontrolled portion of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture XIAFLEX clinical studies, of the 1082 patients who received 0.58 &#x0A;mg of XIAFLEX (2630 XIAFLEX injections), there were 3 patients (0.3%) who experienced a flexor tendon rupture of the treated finger within 7 days of the injection. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 This section of the XIAFLEX PI describes &#x0A;reactions that occurred during the clinical trials program for XIAFLEX in Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. Studies 1 and 2 (CORD I and CORD II) were the clinical trials that supported the approval of XIAFLEX for the treatment of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. In Study &#x0A;1 and Study 2, patients were treated with up to 3 injections of 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX or placebo with approximately 4-week intervals between injections. Patients had finger extension procedures the day after injection, if needed, to facilitate disruption &#x0A;of the cord. The 2 studies were composed of 374 patients; 249 received 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX and 125 received placebo. Participants had a mean age of 63 years; 100% of participants were white, ~80% were male, and ~20% were female. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Because clinical studies are conducted under widely varying conditions, adverse reaction rates observed in the clinical studies of a drug cannot be directly compared to the rates in the clinical studies of another drug and may not reflect the rates observed in practice. &#x0A;In the controlled and uncontrolled portion of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture XIAFLEX clinical studies, of the 1082 patients who received 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX (2630 XIAFLEX injections), there were 3 patients (0.3%) who experienced a flexor tendon rupture of the treated finger within 7 days of the injection. &#x0A;This section of the XIAFLEX PI describes reactions that occurred during the clinical trials program for XIAFLEX in Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. Studies 1 and 2 (CORD I and CORD II) were the clinical trials that supported the approval of XIAFLEX for the treatment of Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. In Study 1 and Study 2, patients were treated with up to 3 injections of 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX or placebo with approximately 4-week intervals between injections. Patients had finger extension procedures the day after injection, if needed, to facilitate disruption of the cord. The 2 studies were composed of 374 patients; 249 received 0.58 mg of XIAFLEX and 125 received placebo. Participants had a mean age of 63 years; 100% of participants were white, ~80% were male, and ~20% were female. </raw>
