<html>span.text1807007Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807007Font1&quot;  &gt;Additional studies were also conducted. An observational, open-label study called Study 4 (known as CORDLESS) was conducted in subjects who had participated in XIAFLEX clinical trials for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. A subset of patients who had recurrence of contracture in a joint that was previously successfully treated with XIAFLEX in Study 4 was retreated in Study 5 (known as the Retreatment Study). &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807007Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1807007Font1&quot;  &gt;No new safety signals were identified among subjects who were retreated with XIAFLEX. A safety signal is a newly observed piece of information that arises from clinical trials or clinical practice that suggests a potentially causal association between an intervention (such as drug treatment) and a safety event that is judged to merit further investigation. &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql Additional studies were also conducted. An observational, open-label study called Study 4 (known as CORDLESS) was conducted in subjects who had participated in XIAFLEX clinical trials for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. A subset of patients &#x0A;who had recurrence of contracture in a joint that was previously successfully treated with XIAFLEX in Study 4 was retreated in Study 5 (known as the Retreatment Study).  \par\par No new safety signals were identified among subjects who were retreated &#x0A;with XIAFLEX. A safety signal is a newly observed piece of information that arises from clinical trials or clinical practice that suggests a potentially causal association between an intervention (such as drug treatment) and a safety event that is judged &#x0A;to merit further investigation.  \par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Additional studies were also conducted. An observational, open-label study called Study 4 (known as CORDLESS) was conducted in subjects who had participated in XIAFLEX clinical trials for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture. A subset of patients who had recurrence of contracture in a joint that was previously successfully treated with XIAFLEX in Study 4 was retreated in Study 5 (known as the Retreatment Study).  &#x0A;No new safety signals were identified among subjects who were retreated with XIAFLEX. A safety signal is a newly observed piece of information that arises from clinical trials or clinical practice that suggests a potentially causal association between an intervention (such as drug treatment) and a safety event that is judged to merit further investigation.  </raw>
<numoflines>11</numoflines>
