<objquestion id="1364579" parent="1364522" questiontype="multchoice" idtext="1542019" idvar="1364578" idVarAttempts="1364630" allowmultiple="true" persist="true">
<name>Question 1</name>
<lastupdated>1769098952</lastupdated>
<questiontext>Which of the following statements about XIAFLEX immunogenicity are true? Select all that apply. </questiontext>
<actionitem actiontaken="show" target="object" targetobject="1364556">
<browserWnd />
</actionitem>
<actionitemincorrect actiontaken="show" target="object" targetobject="1364548">
<browserWnd />
</actionitemincorrect>
<feedbackmethodcorrect>3</feedbackmethodcorrect>
<feedbackmethodincorrect>3</feedbackmethodincorrect>
<maxallowedattempts>2</maxallowedattempts>
<methodfbformaxattempts>3</methodfbformaxattempts>
<actitemfbformaxattempts actiontaken="show" target="object" targetobject="1364567">
<browserWnd />
</actitemfbformaxattempts>
<objchoice idtext="1542020" idbutton="1542021">
<choicetext>Immunogenicity assay results may be compared between those for XIAFLEX and those for other products containing collagenase clostridium histolyticum. </choicetext>
<feedbackmethod>0</feedbackmethod>
</objchoice>
<objchoice idtext="1542022" idbutton="1542023" correctanswer="true">
<choicetext>Since the protein components in XIAFLEX (AUX-I and AUX-II) have some sequence homology with human matrix metalloproteinases (MMPs), anti-product antibodies could theoretically interfere with human MMPs. </choicetext>
<feedbackmethod>0</feedbackmethod>
</objchoice>
<objchoice idtext="1542024" idbutton="1542025" correctanswer="true">
<choicetext>In vitro studies showed no evidence of cross-reactivity between anti-drug-antibody positive patient sera and a series of relevant MMPs.</choicetext>
<feedbackmethod>0</feedbackmethod>
</objchoice>
<objchoice idtext="1542026" idbutton="1542027" correctanswer="true">
<choicetext>No clinical safety concerns related to the inhibition of endogenous MMPs have been observed. </choicetext>
<feedbackmethod>0</feedbackmethod>
</objchoice>
