<html>span.text1880816Font1 { font-size:21px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#000000; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1880816Font1&quot;  &gt;Core Message Support &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\cf2\fs32\b Core Message Support \par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Core Message Support </raw>
<numoflines>1</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
<text id="1880817" parent="1880802" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" defaulttext="none">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769450410</lastupdated>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>219</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>605</cx>
<cy>241</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1880817Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1880817Font1&quot;  &gt;XIAFLEX has proven efficacy in treating appropriate adult patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture with a palpable cord across a broad range of MP contractures. Results from CORD I and CORD II show a greater proportion of XIAFLEX-treated patients achieved the primary endpoint (77% and 65% for all MP joints [Study 1 and Study 2], respectively) compared to placebo-treated patients (7% and 9% for all MP joints [Study 1 and Study 2], respectively). Note that patients may have received up to 3 injections of study medication into the cords associated with contracture of the primary joints on Days 0, 30, and 60. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1880817Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1880817Font1&quot;  &gt;Assessments were made 30 days after the last injection on Days 30, 60, or 90. XIAFLEX-treated patients received a mean of 1.7 injections in the 90-day controlled period in each clinical trial. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil \fcharset2 Wingdings;}{\f3 \froman \fcharset2 Symbol;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc2 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 XIAFLEX has proven efficacy in treating appropriate adult patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture with a palpable cord across a broad range of MP contractures. Results from CORD I and CORD II show a greater &#x0A;proportion of XIAFLEX-treated patients achieved the primary endpoint (77% and 65% for all MP joints [Study 1 and Study 2], respectively) compared to placebo-treated patients (7% and 9% for all MP joints [Study 1 and Study 2], respectively). Note that &#x0A;patients may have received up to 3 injections of study medication into the cords associated with contracture of the primary joints on Days 0, 30, and 60. \plain\f1\fs24\par\par\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1 Assessments were made 30 days after the last injection &#x0A;on Days 30, 60, or 90. XIAFLEX-treated patients received a mean of 1.7 injections in the 90-day controlled period in each clinical trial. \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿XIAFLEX has proven efficacy in treating appropriate adult patients with Dupuytren&apos;s contracture with a palpable cord across a broad range of MP contractures. Results from CORD I and CORD II show a greater proportion of XIAFLEX-treated patients achieved the primary endpoint (77% and 65% for all MP joints [Study 1 and Study 2], respectively) compared to placebo-treated patients (7% and 9% for all MP joints [Study 1 and Study 2], respectively). Note that patients may have received up to 3 injections of study medication into the cords associated with contracture of the primary joints on Days 0, 30, and 60. &#x0A;Assessments were made 30 days after the last injection on Days 30, 60, or 90. XIAFLEX-treated patients received a mean of 1.7 injections in the 90-day controlled period in each clinical trial. </raw>
<numoflines>12</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
