<html>span.text1881669Font1 { font-size:21px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#000000; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;span.text1881669Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881669Font1&quot;  &gt;Clinical Concept&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881669Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Normal;}{\cs1\cf2\cb1\ulc2 Default Paragraph Font;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\fs32\b Clinical Concept\plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿Clinical Concept</raw>
<numoflines>1</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
<textpublishlang>Inherit</textpublishlang>
<marginsize>0</marginsize>
</text>
<text id="1881670" parent="1881664" visible="false" ontop="true" fixed="true" proportional="false" publishasimage="true" defaulttext="none">
<name>ann_text</name>
<lastupdated>1769450657</lastupdated>
<possize>
<point>
<x>212</x>
<y>197</y>
</point>
<size>
<cx>616</cx>
<cy>271</cy>
</size>
</possize>
<cssclasses>hideMe a_text</cssclasses>
<opacity>100</opacity>
<html>span.text1881670Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text1881670Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;span.text1881670Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#0000ff; font-weight:bold; text-decoration:underline;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font1&quot;  &gt;The XIAFLEX PI includes patient counseling recommendations for HCPs. HCPs should explicitly share all of the information contained within the Patient Counseling Information section of the PI with their patients. Patients should be advised of the potential for serious complications with XIAFLEX injection for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture (eg, tendon rupture, serious ligament damage, or skin lacerations) and that injection is likely to cause swelling, bruising, bleeding, and/or pain at and around the injection site. &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font1&quot;  &gt;After the injection, patients should be advised not to flex or extend the fingers of the injected hand or attempt to disrupt the injected cords; to elevate the injected hand until bedtime; to contact their physician without delay for any evidence of infection, sensory changes, difficulty bending the finger(s), or skin laceration of the injected finger; and to return to their HCP 1 to 3 days after the injection for examination and possible finger extension procedure(s) to disrupt the cord.&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font2&quot;  &gt;Please view the video on XIAFLEX patient counseling &lt;/span &gt;&lt;a href=&quot;##Action 1891847&quot;  &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font3&quot;  &gt;here&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font2&quot;  &gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text1881670Font1&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fnil Verdana;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue255 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf3\cb1\ulc3 ;}{\s3\snext3\fs20\cf3\cb1\ulc3\sa120 +NXL_Table_Bullet;}{\cs4\f2\cf3\cb1\ulc3 +NXL_Table_Bullet Char;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\ql The XIAFLEX PI includes patient counseling recommendations for HCPs. HCPs should explicitly share all of the information contained within the Patient Counseling Information section of the PI with their patients. Patients should &#x0A;be advised of the potential for serious complications with XIAFLEX injection for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture (eg, tendon rupture, serious ligament damage, or skin lacerations) and that injection is likely to cause swelling, bruising, bleeding, and/or pain &#x0A;at and around the injection site. \par\par After the injection, patients should be advised not to flex or extend the fingers of the injected hand or attempt to disrupt the injected cords; to elevate the injected hand until bedtime; to contact their physician &#x0A;without delay for any evidence of infection, sensory changes, difficulty bending the finger(s), or skin laceration of the injected finger; and to return to their HCP 1 to 3 days after the injection for examination and possible finger extension procedure(s) &#x0A;to disrupt the cord.\par\par\b Please view the video on XIAFLEX patient counseling {\field\fldlock{\*\fldinst MERGEFIELD \lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\sshlink\ul  HYPERLINK &quot;##Action 1891847&quot; }{\fldrslt\lang1033\hich\f1\loch\f1\cf2\sshlink\ul here}}. &#x0A; \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿The XIAFLEX PI includes patient counseling recommendations for HCPs. HCPs should explicitly share all of the information contained within the Patient Counseling Information section of the PI with their patients. Patients should be advised of the potential for serious complications with XIAFLEX injection for Dupuytren&apos;s contracture (eg, tendon rupture, serious ligament damage, or skin lacerations) and that injection is likely to cause swelling, bruising, bleeding, and/or pain at and around the injection site. &#x0A;After the injection, patients should be advised not to flex or extend the fingers of the injected hand or attempt to disrupt the injected cords; to elevate the injected hand until bedtime; to contact their physician without delay for any evidence of infection, sensory changes, difficulty bending the finger(s), or skin laceration of the injected finger; and to return to their HCP 1 to 3 days after the injection for examination and possible finger extension procedure(s) to disrupt the cord.&#x0A;Please view the video on XIAFLEX patient counseling here.  </raw>
<numoflines>15</numoflines>
<numpubbullets>0</numpubbullets>
