<html>span.text363923Font1 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#179dc0; font-weight:bold;}&#x0A;span.text363923Font2 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101;}&#x0A;span.text363923Font3 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#179dc0; font-weight:bold; font-style:italic;}&#x0A;span.text363923Font4 { font-size:16px; font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;, sans-serif; color:#010101; font-style:italic;}&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font1&quot;  &gt;immunogenicity &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt;capacity to induce a detectable immune response &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font1&quot;  &gt;immunoglobulin E (IgE) &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt;immunoglobulin that attaches to mast cells in the respiratory and intestinal tracts and plays a major role in allergic reactions; about 50% of patients with allergies have increased IgE levels &amp;nbsp;&#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font3&quot;  &gt;in vitro &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt;in glass, ie, a test tube; an &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font4&quot;  &gt;in vitro&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt; test is one done in the laboratory, usually involving isolated tissue, organ, or cell preparations &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font3&quot;  &gt;in vivo &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt;in the living body or organism; an &lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font4&quot;  &gt;in vivo&lt;/span &gt;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt; test is one performed on a living organism &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font1&quot;  &gt;intralesional &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363923Font2&quot;  &gt;within a lesion &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fswiss \fcharset0 Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red23\green157\blue192 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc3 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\pard\s0\ltrpar\ql\widctlpar\hich\f2\loch\f2\cf2\b immunogenicity \par\plain\f2\fs24\par capacity to induce a detectable immune response \par\par\cf2\b immunoglobulin E (IgE) \par\plain\f2\fs24\par immunoglobulin that attaches to mast &#x0A;cells in the respiratory and intestinal tracts and plays a major role in allergic reactions; about 50% of patients with allergies have increased IgE levels  \par\par\cf2\b\i in vitro \par\plain\f2\fs24\par in glass, ie, a test tube; an \i in vitro\plain\f2\fs24 &#x0A; test is one done in the laboratory, usually involving isolated tissue, organ, or cell preparations \par\par\cf2\b\i in vivo \par\plain\f2\fs24\par in the living body or organism; an \i in vivo\plain\f2\fs24  test is one performed on a living organism \par\par\cf2\b &#x0A;intralesional \par\plain\f2\fs24\par within a lesion \plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
<raw>﻿immunogenicity &#x0A;&#x0A;capacity to induce a detectable immune response &#x0A;&#x0A;immunoglobulin E (IgE) &#x0A;&#x0A;immunoglobulin that attaches to mast cells in the respiratory and intestinal tracts and plays a major role in allergic reactions; about 50% of patients with allergies have increased IgE levels  &#x0A;&#x0A;in vitro &#x0A;&#x0A;in glass, ie, a test tube; an in vitro test is one done in the laboratory, usually involving isolated tissue, organ, or cell preparations &#x0A;&#x0A;in vivo &#x0A;&#x0A;in the living body or organism; an in vivo test is one performed on a living organism &#x0A;&#x0A;intralesional &#x0A;&#x0A;within a lesion </raw>
