rest the point of attachment, to the center of the body, or to the point of reference; the opposite of distal &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363930Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363930Font1&quot;  &gt;pruritus &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363930Font2&quot; style=&quot;background-color:transparent&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;&lt;p  legLH=&quot;1.127&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:0px;text-indent:0px;line-height:1.080;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px;text-align:left;&quot; &gt;&#x0A;&lt;span class=&quot;text363930Font2&quot;  &gt;tingling or faintly burning skin sensation that prompts a person to rub or scratch; an itch; it may be a symptom of a disease such as hyperbilirubinemia, an allergic response, or an insect bite &#x0A;&lt;/span &gt;&lt;/p &gt;&#x0A;</html>
<rtf>{\rtf1\ansi\deflang1033\ftnbj\uc1\deff1&#x0A;{\fonttbl{\f0 \froman \fcharset0 Times New Roman;}{\f1 \fswiss Arial;}{\f2 \fswiss \fcharset0 Arial;}}&#x0A;{\colortbl\red0\green0\blue0 ;\red255\green255\blue255 ;\red23\green157\blue192 ;\red0\green0\blue0 ;}&#x0A;{\stylesheet{\f1\fs24\cf2\cb1\ulc3 Normal;}{\cs1\cf3\cb1\ulc3 Default Paragraph Font;}{\s2\snext0\cf2\cb1\ulc3 ;}}&#x0A;{\*\revtbl{Unknown;}}&#x0A;\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\headery720\footery720\deftab360\formshade\aendnotes\aftnnrlc\pgbrdrhead\pgbrdrfoot&#x0A;\sectd\pgwsxn12240\pghsxn15840\marglsxn1800\margrsxn1800\margtsxn1440\margbsxn1440\headery720\footery720\sbkpage\pgncont\pgndec&#x0A;\plain\plain\f1\fs24\pard\s0\ltrpar\ql\widctlpar\hich\f2\loch\f2\cf2\b palmar \par\plain\f2\fs24\par pertaining to the palm of the hand \par\par\cf2\b palpable  \par\plain\f2\fs24\par perceptible, especially by touch \par\par\cf2\b pharmacokinetics \par\plain\f2\fs24\par &#x0A;study of the metabolism and action of drugs with particular emphasis on the time required for absorption, duration of action, distribution in the body, and method of excretion \par\par\cf2\b pharmacology \par\plain\f2\fs24\par study of drugs and their &#x0A;origin, nature, properties, and effects upon living organisms \par\par\cf2\b plasma \par\plain\f2\fs24\par liquid part of blood and of lymph \par\par\cf2\b presyncope \par\plain\f2\fs24\par sensation that one is about to pass out \par\par\cf2\b proximal \par\plain\f2\fs24\par &#x0A;nearest the point of attachment, to the center of the body, or to the point of reference; the opposite of distal \par\par\cf2\b pruritus \par\plain\f2\fs24\par tingling or faintly burning skin sensation that prompts a person to rub or scratch; an itch; &#x0A;it may be a symptom of a disease such as hyperbilirubinemia, an allergic response, or an insect bite \par\pard\s0\ql\plain\f1\fs24\par}&#x0A;</rtf>
